From 11c482a86e79cbaf5d7cef6dfb11dfe883332c39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:54:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: Re-queue the cursor blink work when the console lock
 is busy

fb_flashcursor() bails out without re-queuing itself when console_trylock()
fails. With a busy serial console (115200 baud, loglevel 7) that happens
often enough during boot that the cursor stops blinking until the next
console write.

Re-queue the work for the next blink interval instead of dropping it. This
does not block, which is what the trylock is there to avoid, and
cancel_delayed_work_sync() in fbcon_del_cursor_work() handles the
self-re-queue on teardown.

Tested on the TrimUI Smart Pro (A133): /sys/class/graphics/fbcon/cursor_blink
(delayed_work_pending of the blink work) stays 1 in 10/10 samples over 20 s
after each of two boots. Before, the blink stopped intermittently at boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
index 23b3c536d..b97273289 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
@@ -402,8 +402,18 @@ static void fb_flashcursor(struct work_struct *work)
 	/* instead we just fail to flash the cursor if we can't get
 	 * the lock instead of blocking fbcon deinit */
 	ret = console_trylock();
-	if (ret == 0)
+	if (ret == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * Try again at the next blink instead of dropping the work for
+		 * good: with a busy serial console the lock is often held, and
+		 * the cursor would stop blinking until the next console write.
+		 * cancel_delayed_work_sync() in fbcon_del_cursor_work() copes
+		 * with the re-queue.
+		 */
+		queue_delayed_work(system_power_efficient_wq, &par->cursor_work,
+				   par->cur_blink_jiffies);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	/* protected by console_lock */
 	info = par->info;
-- 
2.56.0

